---
/**
 * The just-yt logo: the name, and nothing else.
 *
 * There is no mark. A play triangle borrows YouTube's iconography, and an
 * abstract letterform next to a four-word sidebar is decoration standing in for
 * a brand. The package is called `just-yt`; setting that well is the logo.
 *
 * The weight split — `just-` quiet, `yt` at full contrast — is what keeps it
 * from reading as a stray line of text. It's one string to a screen reader and
 * one string on the clipboard; only the colour changes.
 */
---

<span class="logo">
  <span class="quiet">just-</span>yt
</span>

<style>
  .logo {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    /* Tight, because the hyphen already puts a gap in the middle of the word. */
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .quiet {
    color: var(--muted);
    transition: color 0.15s ease;
  }

  /* The whole name comes up to full contrast when it's a live link. */
  :where(a):hover .quiet {
    color: var(--text);
  }
</style>
